# Auth (Sanctum tokens)

Two separate logins: **admin** (Blade, manages shop owners) and **shop owner** (SPA + Sanctum JSON). Do not share sessions, guards, or redirects between them.

Stateless **Bearer** tokens for owners, not SPA cookie sessions. Owner login is email + password. Tokens expire; expose **refresh** so the SPA can rotate.

Existing seller routes (`backend/routes/api.php`):

- `POST /api/auth/login`
- `GET /api/auth/me`, `POST /api/auth/refresh`, `POST /api/auth/logout` (`auth:sanctum`)

```php
// ✅ login returns user + token via service + Form Request
$user = $this->service->authenticate($request->validated());
$token = $this->service->generateToken($user);

// ❌ session login / Auth::attempt + redirect to Blade
```

- Hash passwords (`hashed` cast). Only active users may log in (`is_active`).
- `AuthResource` may include `id`, `name`, `email`, `phone`, `shopName`, `role`, `locale` — never `password`.
- Refresh must **invalidate the old token** and return a new one (see `AuthTest`).
- SPA: store token + user; send `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. `ProtectedRoute` must use real auth state, not a hardcoded `true`.
- Blade admin (`AdminAuthController`, seller CRUD) creates and manages owners (`is_active`, shop fields). Owners cannot access admin.
- Open self-registration (`POST /api/auth/register` in tests) is **not** the default: prefer admin-provisioned owners unless the user asks for self-signup.
